-- title:
--   Ordered stage decoding preserves normalized means
-- statement:
--   Let $r,s\ge0$ and $N\ge1$ be integers, put $m=r+s+2$, and choose a designated coordinate $j\in\{0,\ldots,m-1\}$. Let $F$ be any real function of an $r$-stage Cauchy–Schwarz parameter and an $s$-tuple in $\mathbb Z/N\mathbb Z$. If $\Phi_j^{\mathrm{ord}}(x)=(a(x),y(x),\ldots)$ is the ordered stage decoder of the AP cube point $x$, then
--   $$
--   \mathbb E_{a,y}F(a,y)=\mathbb E_x F(a(x),y(x)).
--   $$
--   All averages are normalized finite averages. Thus the decoder preserves the double mean while integrating out its unused cube fibers.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/plby/lean-proofs/blob/8822f7ddef30fadbd92e1c6ab4ed897af356af5e/src/latest/Wikipedia/GreenTao/Transference/RelativeCountingDecoderStep.lean#L1331-L1367

